;; Exact-once fire audit (docs/stats.md; docs/incremental.md §8): on this
;; 4-edge chain the instantiation counts are hand-computable -- the copy
;; rule has one satisfying assignment per edge (4) and the transitive rule
;; one per (path(x,y), edge(y,z)) pair: y=2 gives 1, y=3 gives 2, y=4
;; gives 3, so 6 -- and semi-naive evaluation must fire each EXACTLY once.
;; stats-tests.sh asserts the $stat_fires rows against these numbers.

table (edge int int)
table (path int int)

rule (edge 1 2) (edge 2 3) (edge 3 4) (edge 4 5)
rule (path x y) <-- (edge x y)
rule (path x z) <-- (path x y) (edge y z)
